# MovieRecommender2 — project context

## Goal

Stream MovieLens 25M dataset events through Kafka, persist interaction data in Postgres, index movie catalog features in OpenSearch for search, and serve personalized recommendations via retrieve-then-rank (content kNN + NeuMF on ratings).

## Dataset (`datasets/ml-25m/`, mounted at `/data` in Compose)

| File | Schema | Status |
|------|--------|--------|
| `ratings.csv` | userId, movieId, rating, timestamp | **In pipeline** (producer → Kafka → consumer → Postgres) |
| `tags.csv` | userId, movieId, tag, timestamp | **In pipeline** |
| `movies.csv` | movieId, title, genres (~62k rows) | **Bootstrap** via `seed-catalog` → `catalog_movies` |
| `links.csv` | movieId, imdbId, tmdbId | **Bootstrap** via `seed-catalog` (tmdb_id on catalog rows) |

## Architecture

```text
ratings/tags → Kafka producer → Kafka → consumer → Postgres (events)
tag_events → rollup-tags → catalog_movies.tags (pending when tags change)

movies.csv + links.csv → seed-catalog → catalog_movies (Postgres, source of truth)
enrich-tmdb → TMDB API → catalog_movies TMDB columns
index-catalog → catalog_movies → embedder :8100 → OpenSearch movies_v4 → alias `movies`

recommender-api POST /movies → catalog_movies (pending_sync=true)
catalog-indexer-api POST /index/movie/{id} → catalog_movies + embedder → OpenSearch
index-sync (Job) → pending catalog_movies → embedder → OpenSearch alias

recommender-api GET /search → lexical multi_match (title^3, clean_title^2, tagline^1.5, overview^1, tmdb_keywords^1, tags^1); no vote/popularity boost
recommender-api GET /search/similar → embedder + kNN with function_score (popularity, vote_average); optional genre + min_vote_count
recommender-api search hits → movie_id, title, year, genres, overview, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, popularity, score
recommender-api POST /recommend → kNN candidates + NeuMF ranker (planned)
```

**Interview line:** Postgres `catalog_movies` is the catalog source of truth (ML-25m seed + API writes); OpenSearch is a search projection built from Postgres with embeddings. User events still stream via Kafka.

## Current stack

- **Kafka**, **Postgres 17**, **OpenSearch 2.19**
- **Producer / consumer** — ratings & tags; DLQ; health on `:8080`
- **Embedder** — `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`; `POST /embed`, `/health` on `:8100`
- **Indexing** — `seed-catalog`, `enrich-tmdb`, `rollup-tags`, `index-catalog` (Postgres → OpenSearch), `index-sync`; all writes via `build_index_document`
- **Postgres** — `ratings_events`, `tag_events`, `dead_letter_events`, **`catalog_movies`** (base + TMDB enrichment columns)
- **recommender-api** — `GET /search`, `GET /search/similar`, `POST /movies`, `GET /catalog/pending-sync`, `POST /recommend` (planned), `/health` on `:8000`
- **catalog-indexer-api** — `POST /index/movie/{id}` on `:8101`

### Compose profiles

| Profile | Services |
|---------|----------|
| `stream` / `ratings` / `tags` | Kafka pipeline |
| `catalog` | `seed-catalog`, `enrich-tmdb`, `rollup-tags`, `embedder`, `index-catalog`, `index-sync`, `create-movie-index`, `index-movies` |
| `api` | `embedder`, `recommender-api`, `catalog-indexer-api` (+ `migrate`) |

**Runbook:**
1. `docker compose up migrate` (includes catalog_movies TMDB columns)
2. Set `TMDB_API_KEY` in `services/indexing/.env`; set `INDEX_VERSION=v4` and `RECREATE_INDEX=true` when rebuilding locally
3. `docker compose --profile catalog up --build seed-catalog` (movies.csv + links.csv → catalog_movies)
4. `docker compose --profile catalog up --build enrich-tmdb` (TMDB → catalog_movies)
5. Stream tags: `docker compose --profile tags up producer-tags consumer-tags` (fills `tag_events`)
6. `docker compose --profile catalog run rollup-tags` (top user tags → `catalog_movies.tags`)
7. `docker compose --profile catalog up --build embedder index-catalog` (catalog_movies → OpenSearch v4)
8. `docker compose --profile api up --build recommender-api` (embedder, catalog-indexer-api, API)
9. Test: `GET /search?q=toy+story`, `GET /search/similar?movie_id=1&genre=Animation`, `POST /movies?sync=immediate=true`
10. After new tags stream in: `docker compose --profile catalog run rollup-tags` → `docker compose --profile catalog run index-sync`
11. Async catalog: `POST /movies` → `docker compose --profile catalog run index-sync`

## Recommendation model (target)

Personalized recommendations for a user who picks ~5 liked movies (with ratings). **Retrieve wide, rank narrow** — not lexical∩vector intersect.

### Flow

```text
POST /recommend  { seeds: [{movie_id, rating}, ...] }
        │
        ├─► RETRIEVAL (~100–200 candidates)
        │     • Content: avg seed OpenSearch embeddings → kNN (plot/theme similarity)
        │     • Later: CF candidates from Postgres co-rating patterns
        │     • Union + dedupe; exclude seeds and already-rated
        │
        ├─► RANK (score each candidate)
        │     • NeuMF: MF dot-product + MLP, trained on ratings_events
        │
        └─► Top 10 by predicted rating
```

Lexical search is for `GET /search` (typed query), not required when the user only picks seed movies.

### Two embedding systems (different jobs)

| System | Source | Trained on | Used for |
|--------|--------|------------|----------|
| **Content** | embedder on `embedding_text` (clean_title, genres, tags, tagline, overview, keywords; no year) | Pre-trained MiniLM | OpenSearch kNN — similar plot/theme |
| **CF** | NeuMF `user_embedding` + `movie_embedding` (64d) | `ratings_events` (ML-25m) | Predict rating — “would *you* like it?” |

Content **retrieves** candidates; CF **ranks** them. TMDB scalars (`vote_average`, `popularity`, `runtime`, `original_language`) are indexed for filters/boosts, not stuffed into content or CF embeddings.

### Ranker: NeuMF (single model, MF + NN)

One network trained end-to-end on `(user_id, movie_id, rating)`:

```text
user_id  → Embedding → user_vec [64]
movie_id → Embedding → movie_vec [64]
predicted = dot(user_vec, movie_vec) + MLP(concat(user_vec, movie_vec))
```

- **Training (offline):** backprop on all ratings; vectors learn taste from co-rating patterns (no overview/genres in basic v1).
- **Inference:** known user → `user_embedding[user_id]`; cold start (5 picks) → `user_vec = weighted_avg(movie_embedding[seed] × rating)`; score each candidate; sort.
- CF does not “know” genre/plot — it learns “users with your rating pattern liked movie X.” Content kNN covers new/rare movies with little rating history.

### Phased build

| Phase | Deliverable | Neural? |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| **1** | `POST /recommend` — kNN retrieval + heuristic ranker (similarity + votes + genres) | Content embedder only |
| **2** | Index TMDB scalars; TMDB lookup on all ingest paths (incl. `index-sync`) | Same |
| **3** | Train NeuMF on `ratings_events`; serve as ranker (batch job + model artifacts) | CF NeuMF |
| **4** | CF retriever from Postgres; optional hybrid features in ranker | Same + richer |

### OpenSearch vs app code

| Job | OpenSearch | recommender-api / Postgres |
|-----|------------|----------------------------|
| kNN retrieval | ✅ | Build avg seed vector, call OS |
| Lexical search | ✅ | `GET /search` only |
| Filters / vote boost | ✅ `function_score` | Build query |
| Co-rating CF retrieval | ❌ | Postgres on `ratings_events` |
| NeuMF scoring | ❌ | Load saved embeddings + MLP |
| Train NeuMF | ❌ | Offline training job |

**Interview line:** Retrieve with content similarity in OpenSearch, rank with a neural collaborative filter (MF + MLP) trained on streaming ratings — semantic candidates plus “users who rated like you” patterns baked into CF embeddings.

